    "https://www.timeshighereducation.com/unijobs/listing/416787/lecturer-law/": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Law",
      "description": "Lecturer, Law job with SWINBURNE UNIVERSITY OF TECHNOLOGY | 416787 Skip to main content News Rankings Jobs Study abroad Events Resources Solutions Skip to main menu Skip to user menu Jobseekers: Login Sign up Employers: Login (This link will open in a new window) Post a\n                          job (This link will open in a new window) Employers Jobs Home Find a job Job alerts Upload CV Careers advice the.com (This link will open in a new window) More Results Lecturer, Law Employer SWINBURNE UNIVERSITY OF TECHNOLOGY Location Hawthorn, Australia Closing date 11 Nov 2026 View more categories View less categories Academic Discipline Law , Social Sciences Job Type Academic Posts , Lecturers / Assistant Professors Contract Type Permanent Hours Full Time Apply on website Save job Click to add the job to your shortlist You need to sign in or create an account to save a job. Send job Job Details Shape the next generation of legal professionals Full-time, ongoing position at our Hawthorn campus Academic Level B salary + 17% super and staff benefit About the Role Join Swinburne Law School and be part of a collaborative academic community that values personalised education, innovative teaching and research with real-world impact. As a Lecturer, Law, you’ll deliver engaging lectures, tutorials and workshops across undergraduate and postgraduate programs that help students connect legal theory with real-world practice. You’ll contribute to curriculum development and program innovation, using contemporary teaching approaches to create a personalised and supportive learning experience. You’ll also play an active role in Swinburne’s research culture, producing high-quality publications, contributing to research collaborations, and seeking research funding. Alongside your teaching and research, you’ll support and mentor students, contribute to School activities and build strong connections with government, business, communities and the legal profession, both in Australia and internationally. Swinburne Law School is committed to high-quality, personalised education and a vibrant research environment, with opportunities for international collaboration, competitive grants and research that makes a difference. If you’re passionate about legal education, committed to research excellence and excited by the opportunity to make a meaningful contribution to the legal profession, we’d love to hear from you. About You You’re an enthusiastic and collaborative legal academic who brings a commitment to excellent teaching, meaningful research and strong industry connections. You enjoy finding innovative ways to engage students, to work with colleagues to improve learning outcomes, and to contribute to a supportive academic community. To be successful in this role: You’ll bring a passion for legal education and have experience in teaching and developing undergraduate [GL2.1][NL2.2]law programs. You’re confident coordinating subjects and managing associated academic responsibilities. You’re able to teach in one or more of the Priestley 11 prescribed areas of knowledge. Experience in public law, procedural law, family law or mediation and arbitration would be a bonus. You’re excited by the opportunity to make learning engaging and relevant, using innovative teaching approaches such as blended and online learning, case studies, role-plays and simulations to bring legal concepts to life. You’re committed to producing meaningful research that contributes to your discipline. You bring experience in legal research methods and a track record of publishing in quality academic journals. Swinburne is a University of Technology, so a research agenda with a technology slant is an advantage. You’re a confident communicator who can connect with a diverse range of people, from students and academic colleagues to industry partners and other external stakeholders. You’ll thrive in a collaborative environment, enjoy sharing ideas and working towards common goals, and can help coordinate and support a teaching team to deliver an outstanding student experience. You’re keen to grow your research impact and bring the potential to build the capability to attract external funding or to contribute to funded research projects. You’ll value the connection between legal education and professional practice, building relationships with relevant organisations, industries and the legal profession. Qualifications A doctoral qualification in law is essential. A teaching qualification and/or membership of an appropriate professional body would be advantageous. About Swinburne University of Technology Swinburne’s strategy draws upon our understanding of future challenges. We choose to build Swinburne as the prototype of a new and different university – one that is truly of Technology, of Innovation and of Entrepreneurship. We are committed to a differentiated university proposition in education and research. Our Ad Astra strategy is the cornerstone of Swinburne’s bold ambition to lead globally in technology-driven education and research. This strategy positions us to create transformative solutions, empower learners, and partner with industry to thrive in an ever-changing world. What We Offer You! Work your way with flexible working arrangements, including hybrid options and generous parental leave to support a balanced lifestyle. Exclusive staff discounts, including discounted Medibank health insurance, 50% off Swinburne courses and other partner offers. Swinburne offers 17% super and salary packaging options, including car leasing and extra super contributions. Want to learn more? Head over to our benefits page ! To Apply Please submit your CV and cover letter addressing the Key Selection Criteria and your suitability for this position. To review the Position Description and to apply, please scroll down to the bottom of the page. If you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to Swinburne’s Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children Check. If you are experiencing technical difficulties with your application, please contact the Talent Acquisition team at talentacquisition@swin.edu.au Applications Close: Wednesday 11 November 2026, at 11.00pm Swinburne offers flexible working options contained in our leave and parenting/carer policies to support work-life balance. Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Swinburne has become a world-class university, driving social and economic impacts through science, technology, and innovation. As a dual-sector university, our vision is for people and technology working together to build a better world. Central to our vision is our commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion. We pride ourselves on being an equal opportunity employer focused on attracting, retaining, and developing great talent. We work to remove barriers related to gender identity, culture, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability, and age. Swinburne is proud to be recognised as an AWEI Gold Employer, reflecting our commitment to creating an inclusive workplace where LGBTQIA+ employees, students and communities can thrive. We strongly encourage applicants from diverse Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander communities. Our Moondani Toombadool Centre leads our Indigenous education and culture at Swinburne, guided by community wisdom and leadership. We support applicants with disabilities, and reasonable adjustments can be requested at any stage of the recruitment process. For reasonable adjustment requests - including accessible formats of the position description, application form, or other documents, please contact talentacquisition@swin.edu.au or call +61 3 9214 3550. Please note: this phone number is for disability and reasonable adjustment enquiries only. General enquiries about the role can also be emailed to talentacquisition@swin.edu.au . Victoria’s Commitment to Action: Improving international student employment outcomes. As a signatory to Victoria’s Commitment to Action, Swinburne seeks to remove barriers to international graduate employment. We welcome and encourage applications from international graduates. As a Circle Back Initiative Employer, we commit to responding to every applicant. Please click here for Position Description How to apply: Start your application by clicking the \"begin\" button. Login to an existing account or reset your password View our FAQ section View Hints & Tips to help with your application Preview Application Form By choosing to continue, you agree to the privacy policy. Show Privacy Policy Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Apply on website Send job Apply on website Save job Click to add the job to your shortlist You need to sign in or create an account to save a job. Get job alerts Create a job alert and receive personalised job recommendations straight to your inbox. Create alert Similar jobs University Assistant Predoctoral, Law Vienna (Landbezirke) (AT) Senior Lecturer in Law (Criminal Law) Liverpool, United Kingdom University Assistant Predoctoral, Law Vienna (Landbezirke) (AT) back to top Facebook (This link will open in a new window) Twitter (This link will open in a new window) LinkedIn (This link will open in a new window) Contact us Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy © 2015 - 2026 THE World Universities Insights Limited. Powered by Madgex Job Board Software Close Before you apply - Turn on alerts for jobs like this! We'll send them straight to your inbox : What is your email address? required When you create this job alert we will email you a selection of jobs matching your criteria. Our terms and conditions and privacy policy apply to this service and you can unsubscribe at any time. By clicking to continue to apply below, your email address will be shared with the employer. No thanks, continue to apply (This will open in a new window from which you will be automatically redirected to an external site after 5 seconds) Create alert and continue to apply (This will open in a new window from which you will be automatically redirected to an external site after 5 seconds) Madgex Design System Icon. Madgex Design System Icon."
    },
